<title>ZIMBABWE: TABLE - DUNLOP RAISES HALF-YR SHR, DIV.</title>
<headline>TABLE - DUNLOP RAISES HALF-YR SHR, DIV.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-yr to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		(million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)	     10.6     vs     3.8</p>
<p>    Interim div (cts)    3.0     vs     1.8</p>
<p>    Pre-tax earnings    17.6     vs    12.6</p>
<p>    Tax			4.5     vs     7.8</p>
<p>    Exceptional items    6.9     vs     5.1</p>
<p>    Attrib earnings     12.7     vs     4.5</p>
<p>    Sales		  238.3     vs   234.7</p>
<p>Div payable September 26</p>
<p>on register August 29.</p>
<p>Full Name: Dunlop Zimbabwe Limited</p>
<p>Note:- The company said it would continue restructuring its operations with the distribution activities of its Harare-based operations now being consolidated under one roof.</p>
<p>It said it was well placed to take advantage of available market opportunities and to successfully implement the next phase of its capital investment programme. It anticipated that the results from the second six months of trading would exceed those of the first half.</p>
<p>-- Harare Newsroom 263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
</text>
